  "id": "DrugBank_DB01367 - MONDO_18466",
  "verbalization": "Rasagiline is implicated in the pathogenesis of Hereditary Late Onset Parkinson Disease (HLOPD) through a series of indirect pathways. The evidence suggests that Rasagiline may exert its effects through the treatment of Atypical Juvenile Parkinsonism and Early-onset Parkinsonism-intellectual Disability Syndrome, both of which are associated with Cycrimine. These conditions are linked to HLOPD, indicating a potential role for Rasagiline in the management of late-onset Parkinsonism. The integration of these pathways highlights a possible mechanism by which Rasagiline could influence the progression of HLOPD, though the exact mechanism remains to be fully elucidated. The evidence supports a connection between Rasagiline and HLOPD through a chain of indications, suggesting a broader therapeutic relevance in late-onset Parkinsonism.",
